YOUR IDENTITY DID NOT REACH THE TOOL, so nothing on the record binds this agent to this seat. You are registered and your events are recorded; what is missing is the binding that lets a LATER call resolve who you are without being told.

TWO CONSEQUENCES:
  PASS --seat-id ON EVERY CALL. Without it the tool cannot tell which seat is asking and will refuse you.
  REGISTERING AGAIN WILL NOT FIX IT. If a later call says "this agent has not registered", it is THIS, not a lost registration — and a second register cannot supply an agent id the hook never sent. Your work is safe either way; the record is append-only and keeps both sittings.

